{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::4718",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is shown to interact with Ndufa12 and Ndufv3, both of which are subunits of the Nadh dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) complex, and Ndufc2 is a subunit of the same complex. This suggests that Metformin may modulate the activity of this enzyme complex, potentially through direct binding to Ndufa12 or Ndufv3. The evidence from the three paths indicates a consistent mechanism where Metformin influences the activity of the Nadh dehydrogenase complex, which in turn affects Ndufc2. The high scores in all three paths suggest a strong and reliable relationship, though the exact mechanism of Metformin's interaction with Ndufa12 and Ndufv3 remains to be fully elucidated. The observed effect on Ndufc2 is likely a downstream consequence of the modulation of the Nadh dehydrogenase activity, which is a well-documented pathway in cellular respiration. This integrated evidence supports the hypothesis that Metformin may exert its therapeutic effects through this mechanism, though further studies are needed to confirm the precise role of Ndufa12 and Ndufv3 in this process.",
